  "ssml.intro": "SSML is used only when the orange SSML mode is active. Plain text remains the default. Language segments keep the current voice; voice segments create characters and multilingual dialogue.",
  "ssml.voiceHelp": "Switch voices between dialogue turns. The voice selects its native language unless a nested language is explicit.",
  "ssml.languageHelp": "Use another language frontend while preserving the current voice and its character.",
  "ssml.prosodyHelp": "Style one segment. Every attribute is optional; omitted or blank values inherit unchanged.",
  "ssml.breakHelp": "Set the complete pause at this boundary, up to 10 seconds. Use 0ms for no gap; adjacent turns without a break use 100ms.",
  "ssml.subHelp": "Speak the alias instead of the label.",
  "ssml.charactersHelp": "Read characters separately.",
  "ssml.numberHelp": "Read a numeric value normally.",
  "ssml.ordinalHelp": "Read an English ordinal. Experimental English voices only.",
  "ssml.phonemeHelp": "Use Kokoro/eSpeak-compatible IPA directly.",
  "ssml.limits": "Prosody ranges are speed and tempo 0.5-2, pitch -12st to +12st, and volume 0-2. Nested values compose with request-level controls and must remain in range. Loudness normalization remains request-wide. One speak root is required. Voice names must be enabled. Language tags accept served Kokoro codes and common BCP-47 forms. Documents are limited to 50,000 characters, 256 elements, and eight nesting levels; direct phonemes to 510 characters and ordinals to 18 digits. Unsafe or unsupported input is rejected.",
